&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team develops unmanned aerial systems capable of terminal guidance, long range intelligence collection, precision navigation, and unsupervised autonomy. Anvil, Altius, Ghost, and other developmental UAS platforms are built to operate in remote environments with limited user input, driving requirements for reliability and autonomy. We have developed an autonomy stack that receives user intent, responds to detections processed at the edge, and coordinates flight patterns for groups of assets. We are looking for entry level graduates who are eager to learn the Anduril-way and quickly develop their skills to contribute in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable UAS C2 capabilities through resilient network design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive system/subsystem/component level requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop and maintain system components in complex system environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document software engineering processes and networking best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the deployment, configuration, and maintenance of lab and flight-test networking hardware, including tactical radios, switches, routers, and edge compute nodes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) integration and bench testing to validate network reliability and throughput for command-and-control (C2) and sensor data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain physical and virtual test setups to simulate contested, high-latency, or bandwidth-constrained network environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors Degree in STEM (Electrical Engineering, Mechanical, Aerospace, Physics, Computer Science or other relevant engineering discipline)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for networking, system design, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with basic networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership and impact from internships, side projects, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go-getter mentality who is eager to learn from Anduril&#39;s best and brightest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extremely organized and detail-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal &amp;amp; written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sincere commitment to a positive, inclusive, and collaborative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain a DoD Security Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a network engineer that highlights your ability to execute engineering level tasks as an individual and part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Linux based operating systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with test script development using common languages (Python, Matlab etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with RF Integration with, but not limited to, Unmanned Aerial Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tactical radios&lt;/li&gt;
