&lt;li&gt;Correct major and minor discrepancies by removal, repair, or replacement of defective avionics, electrical, payloads and subsystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform scheduled maintenance and functional checks on aircraft avionics, electrical, and subsystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to fabricate, upgrade and modify aircraft harnesses, coax cables and fiber optic as well as install and checkout with limited engineering guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Load and maintain software configuration on Aircraft and Ground Segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with software loads and regressions in a development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upkeep of DTED, WX, Aeronautical Charts, and other supporting information for GCS mission planning systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, repair, and maintain aircraft and subsystems including landing gear, fuel system, flight control, and propulsion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct a variety of aircraft ground operations including Launch, Recovery, and Ground Engine run-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform standard preflight maintenance on prototype and experimental aircraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete aircraft and equipment documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate avionics assessment with engineering and manufacturing personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform proper FOD and tool control practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and teamwork abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with computer use (standard browser, word processing applications).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience and training in Install, troubleshooting and checkout of flight test instrumentation systems to include but not limited to strain gauges, excels, strain pots and all associated wiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable to perform tasks independently, manage time effectively, and make decisions without constant supervision or guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to meticulously interpret and work from engineering drawings and draft procedures, ensuring accuracy in translating technical specifications into practical applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to be multi-capable. Which shall include some electronics troubleshooting and repair.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active TS Clearance, investigation within 5 years or continuous evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 years or more of aircraft avionics experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years or more of developmental flight test experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to rapidly change roles/responsibilities while working in a fast paced, challenging work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as required.&lt;/li&gt;
