&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Staff Threat and Attack Research Engineer to join our Security organization. The ideal candidate will combine threat intelligence knowledge with strong engineering skills to develop and implement advanced threat actor tracking and analysis systems to protect Anduril products and infrastructure. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze sophisticated cyber threats targeting Anduril&#39;s products, infrastructure, and personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, mitigate, and anticipate emerging technical trends in the threat landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the detection and response team to provide timely and actionable intelligence to support ongoing investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage cross functionally with the offensive security team on product and infrastructure red team engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance tooling for threat actor tracking and intelligence data integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster proactive collaboration and information exchange with external partners to build joint capabilities and achieve shared objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience analyzing complex threat actor campaigns, including supply chain and infrastructure, with the ability to develop long term countermeasures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in one or more programming languages (e.g. Python, Rust, Golang, Swift)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to prioritize and execute tasks independently with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and professional communication skills (written and verbal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and hold a U.S. Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of nation-state, sophisticated criminal, or supply chain threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating file-based or network-based rules and signatures (e.g. YARA, Snort) for detection and tracking complex threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of writing production code for threat intelligence tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in large scale data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established connection within the broader security and threat intel community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
