&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part Packaging and Rack Flow:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Develop cost effective and sustainable packaging solutions for use between vendors and SpaceX and within Starbase facilities. Ensure that the packaging optimizes for total landed cost by considering logistics density and handling efficiency, while maintaining required quality standards. Work with external packaging and tooling vendors as well as internal teams to get right-sized packaging fleets built in time to support program targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis and Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Utilize data analysis tools (e.g., Excel, Tableau, SQL) to assess material flow performance metrics, identify issues, and develop data-driven solutions. Support the Materials Management operations teams as needed with decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety and Training:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Conduct risk assessments and implement measures to ensure that all Materials Management processes adhere to federal, state, local and SpaceX safety standards. Conduct periodic audits to ensure that safe conditions do not develop, all processes are being completed per design standards and any equipment in use remains adequate for the process it supports. Develop and lead training for new processes and equipment,&lt;/li&gt;
