&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPPLIER DEVELOPMENT ENGINEER, MATERIALS &amp;amp; METALS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starship needs a supply base that can hold quality while designs change and rates go up. This role is the technical owner for materials and metals at our suppliers — raw material, processing, and special processes that fly on the vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&amp;nbsp;will&amp;nbsp;take&amp;nbsp;hardware&amp;nbsp;from&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;product&amp;nbsp;development&amp;nbsp;through&amp;nbsp;stable&amp;nbsp;production&amp;nbsp;across&amp;nbsp;metal&amp;nbsp;processing,&amp;nbsp;finishing,&amp;nbsp;welding,&amp;nbsp;heat&amp;nbsp;treatment,&amp;nbsp;inspection,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;related&amp;nbsp;processes.&amp;nbsp;You&amp;nbsp;need&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;real&amp;nbsp;materials&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;metallurgy&amp;nbsp;foundation,&amp;nbsp;judgment&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;shop&amp;nbsp;floor,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;willingness&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;pick&amp;nbsp;up&amp;nbsp;unfamiliar&amp;nbsp;work&amp;nbsp;when&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;mission&amp;nbsp;requires&amp;nbsp;it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve&amp;nbsp;as&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;technical&amp;nbsp;point&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;contact&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;materials&amp;nbsp;commodities&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;processes,&amp;nbsp;including&amp;nbsp;raw&amp;nbsp;material,&amp;nbsp;welding,&amp;nbsp;heat&amp;nbsp;treatment,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;finishing/coating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own&amp;nbsp;development&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;raw-material&amp;nbsp;commodities&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;related&amp;nbsp;products:&amp;nbsp;select&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;manufacturing&amp;nbsp;method,&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;vet&amp;nbsp;suppliers,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;build&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;process&amp;nbsp;that&amp;nbsp;can&amp;nbsp;ramp&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve&amp;nbsp;emergent&amp;nbsp;supplier&amp;nbsp;issues&amp;nbsp;that&amp;nbsp;threaten&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;manifest&amp;nbsp;—&amp;nbsp;high-impact&amp;nbsp;materials,&amp;nbsp;processing,&amp;nbsp;manufacturing,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;quality&amp;nbsp;problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead&amp;nbsp;containment&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;materials&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;process&amp;nbsp;escapes:&amp;nbsp;scope&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;risk,&amp;nbsp;align&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;path&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;engineering&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;supply&amp;nbsp;chain,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;drive&amp;nbsp;it&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;root&amp;nbsp;cause&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;materials&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;processing&amp;nbsp;issues;&amp;nbsp;implement&amp;nbsp;fixes&amp;nbsp;at&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;supplier,&amp;nbsp;at&amp;nbsp;SpaceX,&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;disposition&amp;nbsp;issue&amp;nbsp;tickets&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;engineering&amp;nbsp;counterparts&amp;nbsp;(rework,&amp;nbsp;repair,&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;use-as-is)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive&amp;nbsp;requirement&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;drawing&amp;nbsp;changes&amp;nbsp;that&amp;nbsp;cut&amp;nbsp;defect&amp;nbsp;risk,&amp;nbsp;improve&amp;nbsp;manufacturability,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;reduce&amp;nbsp;lead&amp;nbsp;time&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;procurement&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;find&amp;nbsp;capable&amp;nbsp;suppliers&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;assess&amp;nbsp;them&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;quality&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;takt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review&amp;nbsp;supplier&amp;nbsp;manufacturing&amp;nbsp;processes&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;quality&amp;nbsp;systems;&amp;nbsp;push&amp;nbsp;improvements&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;own&amp;nbsp;follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;supply-chain&amp;nbsp;owner&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;materials-&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;process-related&amp;nbsp;defects&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;your&amp;nbsp;commodities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in materials science and engineering, metallurgy, or metallurgical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with R&amp;amp;D, manufacturing, or processing engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with manufacturing, raw materials, special processes, castings, forgings, or sheet metal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with assessing supplier technical capability from an equipment, operations, and personnel perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of supplier quality processes (PPAP, APQP, FAIR, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disciplined approach to problem solving (8D, Pareto, root cause, corrective action, PFMEA, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with quality systems (ISO 9000//AS9100)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of lean concepts and statistical methods (Minitab, DOE, Six Sigma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate with all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence across functions, internally and at the supplier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours, some nights and/or weekends when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel: up to 40-50% work week travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;Level 1: $100,000.00 - $117,500.00&lt;br&gt;Level 2: $115,000.00 - $140,000.00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees accrue paid sick leave pursuant to Company policy which satisfies or exceeds the accrual, carryover, and use requirements of the law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPPLIER DEVELOPMENT ENGINEER, SMT (STARLINK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is developing a low latency, broadband internet system to meet the needs of consumers across the globe. Enabled by a constellation of low Earth orbit satellites, Starlink will provide fast, reliable internet to populations with little or no connectivity, including those in rural communities and places where existing services are too expensive or unreliable. We are looking for talented, creative, and driven engineers to develop, drive, and maintain suppliers, from initial concept development to full scale production.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Supplier Development Engineer focused on Surface Mount Technology (SMT) for Starlink, you will play a critical role in ensuring the quality, reliability, and scalability of PCBA (Printed Circuit Board Assembly) manufacturing at our global suppliers. You will lead New Product Introduction (NPI) efforts, drive process improvements, and manage the ramp-up of SMT production lines to meet SpaceX&#39;s high-volume demands. This position requires deep technical expertise in SMT processes, hands-on experience with PCBA manufacturing, and the ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams and suppliers worldwide. Based in Bastrop, Texas, you will report to the Supplier Development Engineering team lead and contribute to the rapid iteration and production scaling of Starlink hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead supplier qualification, development, and ongoing performance management for SMT and PCBA manufacturing processes to ensure compliance with SpaceX quality standards and production timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive NPI activities for new SMT lines, including process validation, equipment selection, and yield optimization at supplier facilities around the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve manufacturing defects, process inefficiencies, and quality issues in SMT assembly, such as solder paste application, component placement, reflow soldering, and automated optical inspection (AOI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct root cause analysis and implement corrective actions for production failures, utilizing tools like PFMEA, DOE, and SPC to improve process capability and reduce defects per million opportunities (DPMO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with SpaceX design, manufacturing, and quality teams to incorporate DFM/DFA feedback into supplier processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to supplier sites (up to 50%) to audit facilities, oversee ramp-ups, and provide on-site technical support for high-volume SMT production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain supplier scorecards, KPIs, and continuous improvement plans focused on cost reduction, yield enhancement, and supply chain resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the transition from prototype to mass production, including capacity planning, equipment upgrades, and automation integration for SMT lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to industry standards (e.g., IPC-A-610, J-STD-001) and SpaceX-specific requirements for mission-critical electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, manufacturing engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in PCBA manufacturing, with a focus on SMT processes (e.g., screen printing, pick-and-place, reflow, wave soldering, and inspection).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with SMT equipment from manufacturers such as Fuji, Panasonic, DEK, or similar, including programming, maintenance, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in SMT engineering, including leadership roles in supplier development or process engineering for complex consumer electronics systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in advanced SMT technologies, such as fine-pitch components, BGA/CSP assembly, selective soldering, and high-mix/low-volume to high-volume transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with statistical process control (SPC), Six Sigma certification, or Lean manufacturing principles applied to SMT environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of environmental testing and reliability standards for consumer electronics (e.g., vibration, thermal cycling).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the consumer electronics industry, particularly with high volume hardware assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple suppliers and projects simultaneously in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in NPI and production ramp-up for high-volume electronics manufacturing, preferably in consumer electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PCBA failure modes, defect analysis, and quality control methodologies (e.g., 8D, Fishbone, Pareto).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position is based in Bastrop, TX and requires being onsite - remote work not considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work long hours and weekends when needed to meet critical deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel: Up to 50% work week travel may be required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;WELDING AUTOMATION ENGINEER, CHAMBER AND NOZZLE (RAPTOR)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;SpaceX is seeking an engineer with deep expertise in automated welding to&amp;nbsp;create the&amp;nbsp;Raptor engine’s combustion chamber and nozzle.&amp;nbsp;These components feature some of the most complex geometries in rocket propulsion — including intricate regenerative cooling channels, thin-walled high-temperature alloys, and tight-tolerance surfaces that must survive extreme thermal and pressure cycles across hundreds of reuse cycles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You will design, implement, and scale&amp;nbsp;manual&amp;nbsp;and automated welding systems that increase production throughput, improve weld consistency, and reduce defects while enabling rapid design iteration. This role sits at the intersection of propulsion engineering, weld&amp;nbsp;engineering,&amp;nbsp;with aspects of&amp;nbsp;real-time process control, and data-driven quality systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Your work will directly enable rapid iteration and high-volume production of Raptor chambers and nozzles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Develop, deploy and iteratively improve automated welding systems for Raptor combustion chambers and nozzles, including manual and automated arc and beam welding processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Design and optimize automated weld paths, parameters, and sequences for complex geometries in regenerative cooling channels and nozzle structures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Implement weld process control with real-time monitoring of arc characteristics, temperature, seam tracking, and penetration using advanced sensors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Build and maintain data pipelines that capture manufacturing telemetry to enable statistical process control, predictive analytics, and machine learning models for defect reduction and process optimization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Develop fixture and material handling solutions that support high-precision welding in a wide variety of forms and materials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Drive continuous improvement of welding automation through scripting (Python), PLC logic, and advanced process modeling to reduce cycle time and scrap rates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Partner closely with propulsion design, materials, production, and supply chain teams to convert new designs into robust, scalable processes, resolve nonconformances, and drive design changes that improve manufacturability, reliability, and performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with welding processes for complex metallic components&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strong programming skills in Python and experience with industrial automation (robotic welding systems, PLCs, or real-time controllers)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Demonstrated success deploying robotic welding, laser welding, or vision-guided welding systems in production environments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-ownership environment with aggressive schedules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Ability to work well in an integrated and collaborative team environment including daily interactions with technicians, engineers, and managers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Direct experience welding rocket engine chambers, nozzles, or regeneratively cooled hardware&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Expertise in welding of high-performance alloys (nickel and copper alloys, stainless steels) using GTAW, laser, or plasma processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Background in real-time weld monitoring, adaptive control, and closed-loop feedback systems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience with offline robot programming, weld simulation software, and integrating welding cells into larger manufacturing lines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Familiarity with non-destructive evaluation tied to welding (ultrasonic, X-ray, CT, or thermography)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Knowledge of statistical process control, GD&amp;amp;T, and data-driven methods for weld quality prediction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Highly self-motivated with strong organizational and written/oral communication skills – able to prioritize and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment with the ongoing drive for continuous improvement in all aspects of work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able stand for long durations (8 hours minimum) and work directly with hardware on the floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be comfortable stooping, bending, and standing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10% travel in support of launch and test of hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility in working hours to production and launch cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pay Range:&lt;br&gt;Level 1: $100,000.00 - $130,000.00&lt;br&gt;Level 2: $115,000.00 - $160,000.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of your total rewards package at SpaceX. You may also be eligible for long-term incentives, in the form of company stock or long-term cash awards, as well as potential discretionary bonuses and the ability to purchase additional stock at a discount through an Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You will also receive access to comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, paid parental leave, and various other discounts and perks. You may also accrue 3 weeks of paid vacation and will be eligible for 10 or more paid holidays per year. Employees accrue paid sick leave pursuant to Company policy which satisfies or exceeds the accrual, carryover, and use requirements of the law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Marketing Events Manager, International at Anthropic, you will own the execution of events across our international markets that drive pipeline, deepen customer relationships, and build Anthropic&#39;s brand and share of mind in markets where we&#39;re growing fast. You&#39;ll deliver a portfolio ranging from global flagship programs adapted for local markets to brand activations, executive dinners, roundtables, customer summits, and third-party events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on the Marketing Events Team, reports to the Head of International Events, and partners closely with International Sales, regional Field Marketing, Communications, Policy, Product Marketing, and Creative. You&#39;ll bring hands-on operational excellence and a strong eye for brand storytelling, turning plans into experiences that resonate with diverse audiences, from developers to enterprise executives to policymakers. As part of a small team building Anthropic&#39;s international events program, you&#39;ll help create the systems, processes, and playbooks that let it scale across regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute international events that deliver on brand objectives, regional sales priorities, and pipeline targets, while contributing to strategy that supports overall company goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and manage a diverse, multi-country portfolio spanning hosted flagship events, brand activations, industry conferences, and cultural moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt global event programs for international markets, working with the Marketing Events team so programs stay aligned with company-wide strategy while meeting local market needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Creative on event identities, spatial design, and experiential elements that bring Anthropic&#39;s brand to life, ensuring our presence is compelling and consistent across all touchpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee event budgets, vendor relationships, and contract negotiations, ensuring strong ROI across the portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Policy, and Communications to align event messaging and maximize the impact of Anthropic&#39;s presence at industry moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain operational frameworks that keep quality and brand consistency high across regions: speaker and staff briefings, Know Before You Go documentation, and post-event reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide on-site leadership and logistics management, serving as the primary point of contact for all event operations during live experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to innovate on event formats and experiences that differentiate Anthropic in the AI landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of B2B event marketing and management experience, including brand-owned, technical, or innovation-focused events across EMEA and/or APAC, at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a proven track record of executing multi-country event programs that deliver brand impact, and measurable pipeline and revenue results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong portfolio of events, including brand events, that turn a company&#39;s values and positioning into memorable, on-brand experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience activating at premium third-party events, including hospitality at high-end venues, sporting events, and cultural experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are highly organized, with exceptional project management skills and the ability to run multiple complex events at once, often in different markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a collaborative partner who builds strong relationships across International Sales, Marketing, and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong budget and vendor management experience, including local suppliers and multiple currencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the cultural awareness and judgement to adapt events for different markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can operate in a fast-paced environment and maintain calm and effective leadership in high-pressure situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong data analysis skills to measure and report on event success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable with regular travel across EMEA and APAC (approximately 30%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with event technology platforms and meeting scheduling tools (e.g., Splash, Cvent, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked closely with enterprise sales teams and understand the enterprise buying cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with creative teams and agencies on event identities, spatial design, and experiential elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed or mentored other team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a genuine interest in AI technology and care about ensuring that transformative AI systems are developed safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£125,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£125,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a National Security Partnerships Lead to grow and manage our relationships with the U.S. Intelligence Community and with allied intelligence and security services. You will report to the Head of National Security Policy and advise company leadership on intelligence and allied-partner matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help partner security organizations build policies that let them adopt frontier AI quickly and for high-impact missions, while deploying it safely and avoiding incidents. You will also engage U.S. and foreign government officials on the policy frameworks that guide the international distribution and deployment of Anthropic&#39;s models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a portfolio of government partnerships end to end: setting the agenda with senior counterparts, structuring the agreements and channels that govern each relationship, and bringing partner requirements and concerns back into Anthropic&#39;s policy, product, research, and safeguards decisions. You will work closely with our public sector sales, legal, security, and threat intelligence teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead Anthropic&#39;s strategic engagement with U.S. Intelligence Community elements and allied intelligence and security services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help partner security organizations develop the policies and governance that enable rapid, high-impact adoption of frontier AI and safe deployments that avoid incidents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify high-leverage national security deployments with partners, and support our public sector sales team in delivering them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brief senior government security officials in the U.S. and allied capitals on frontier AI capabilities, risks, and Anthropic&#39;s approach to safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engage U.S. and foreign government officials on the national security implications of the international distribution and deployment of Anthropic&#39;s models, and advise company leadership on partner equities in those decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with federal affairs, international policy, communications, and marketing on national security matters, including engagement with the Executive Branch and Congress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel regularly within the U.S. and to allied countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Substantial experience in national security, including work in or with the Intelligence Community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct experience managing relationships with foreign partner governments or services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An active TS/SCI clearance, or one held within the last two years, and the ability to obtain and maintain it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience negotiating formal agreements or partnerships between governments, or between government and industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A working understanding of how intelligence organizations operate, including classification, liaison relationships, and how they adopt new technology, and the ability to get things done within those constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ability to brief senior policymakers and officials clearly, and to explain technical subjects without overstating them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working effectively with cross-functional teams, including technical, sales, policy, trust and safety, legal, security, product, research, and communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated interest and experience in a complex technical subject, ideally AI, though defense technology, cybersecurity, or similar fields also count.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ability to build structure where little exists and to manage competing priorities without waiting for perfect clarity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of experience in national security, including substantial work in or with the Intelligence Community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in a liaison, foreign partnership, or foreign disclosure role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in related private-sector roles, such as at technology, cybersecurity, or defense companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Regional expertise or language skills relevant to allied partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on familiarity with large language models and how they can be misused.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
