&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Claude Code is changing how engineering organizations build software, and most of them need someone to show them how. That&#39;s you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Architects help customers get real work done with Claude Code, Claude Tag (Claude Code as an agent in Slack), and the enterprise admin controls that decide whether a rollout succeeds. You&#39;ll teach customers, partners and Anthropic&#39;s own field teams. Just as important, you&#39;ll train the trainers who carry that knowledge to everyone else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hands-on AI engineers who would rather teach than sell. You&#39;ll work alongside customer engineering organizations, teaching them about Claude Code and shepherding rollouts with advanced admin knowledge. Most weeks you&#39;re in front of an audience with Claude Desktop or a terminal open: thousands of engineers on a public webinar one day, a customer&#39;s platform team in their own conference room the next week, office hours in between. The prep material often reaches you the day before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing quickly this year, scope will grow as new products ship, and the people who join now will shape how it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teach in every format.&lt;/strong&gt; Take a standing rotation on Anthropic&#39;s public webinars in front of thousands of engineers at a time. Lead workshops and multi-day onsites, in person and virtual, built around a customer&#39;s own codebase and questions. Host office hours and multi-week cohorts where engineers, partners, and account teams bring live problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teach the teachers.&lt;/strong&gt; Run train-the-trainer programs for customer technologists and champions, and certify them to deliver Anthropic&#39;s material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower admins.&lt;/strong&gt; Educate enterprise admins on the technical requirements for a strong rollout by guiding them through single sign-on, permissions, connectors, spend controls, data-handling policy, and other advanced topics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build fast with Claude.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn a request into a polished deck, demo repository or plugin within a day, using the tools you teach. Explore new features the day they ship. Pick up a teammate&#39;s material and deliver it as if you wrote it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring field signal back to product.&lt;/strong&gt; Tell the Claude Code, Claude Tag and Cowork teams what customers run into, specifically enough that they can fix it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the technical voice in the room.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with account executives, customer success managers, Applied AI Architects, support engineers and partner leads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel.&lt;/strong&gt; Expect 30 to 50%, in bursts around onsites, workshops and events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years as a software engineer, solutions architect, developer advocate or similar. You still ship code and regularly teach engineering audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current engineering range.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve shipped code other people depend on. You can go deep with a senior engineer anywhere in the stack. You use Claude Code or a similar agentic tool every day and have opinions about it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Big-stage presence.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve held large live audiences. You sound practiced with material you got that morning, and a broken demo doesn’t faze you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Range in one conversation.&lt;/strong&gt; You can go from banter to a rigorous design discussion, and both feel natural.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Care for people.&lt;/strong&gt; You do right by a struggling customer, and you won&#39;t leave a confused room behind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initiative.&lt;/strong&gt; You build things without waiting for permission, and you say when an idea is half-formed, including your manager&#39;s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steadiness&lt;/strong&gt; when priorities shift, timelines are short and colleagues are under pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with ambiguity&lt;/strong&gt; in a fast-moving industry and product suite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A stake in safe AI.&lt;/strong&gt; You care that large organizations deploy AI responsibly, and you want to help them do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You love being on the frontier.&lt;/strong&gt; You want to work at the edge of what’s possible and help define what comes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
