&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Mission Readiness team keeps Anduril systems ready to fight. We build the sustainment backbone behind&lt;br&gt;fielded products — the technical data, provisioning, training, support equipment, and field support concepts&lt;br&gt;that determine whether a system stays mission capable once it leaves our factory. Working across engineering,&lt;br&gt;manufacturing, supply chain, test, and program management, the Mission Readiness team turns development&lt;br&gt;hardware into products the force can actually operate, maintain, and sustain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Logistics Analyst to build the supply support, support equipment, and packaging data for&lt;br&gt;our air and missile defense products being developed for our service customer. Reporting to the Logistics&lt;br&gt;Program Manager, you will produce the logistics product data across three Integrated Product Support elements — Supply Support, Support Equipment, and Packaging, Handling, Storage &amp;amp; Transportation (PHS&amp;amp;T) — building&lt;br&gt;the provisioning data, support equipment data, and ammunition lifecycle documentation that allow this missile&lt;br&gt;to be fielded. You will start from an empty database at contract award and build toward a production-ready&lt;br&gt;logistics baseline over the development effort. &lt;br&gt;This is a data and analysis role. You will spend your time in the government’s logistics modeling and Logistics Product Data tools, working closely with design engineering to pull the data you need, with Product Support Engineering to consume their reliability and maintenance analyses, and with test to prove the baseline holds up against real hardware. You are the person who turns engineering outputs into the datasets and deliverables the customer will use to procure and support the system. This role is in-person at one of our office locations and requires periodic domestic travel (up to 25%) to test sites, government facilities, and supplier locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role produces the logistics product data and deliverables across three IPS elements: Supply Support,&lt;br&gt;Support Equipment, and PHS&amp;amp;T. The Logistics Program Manager retains element accountability and the&lt;br&gt;customer relationship.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supply Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the logistics data baseline. Develop and maintain the Logistics Management Information / Logistics Product Data database per GEIA-STD-0007 — provisioning data, parts cataloging, sparing recommendations, and packaging data. This is the dataset the Army will eventually use to procure and support the system, and you are the analyst building it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catalog the hardware. Establish and maintain National Stock Number, CAGE code, and part number structures; build and maintain provisioning parts lists and the supporting technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compute the sparing position. Produce initial outfitting and sustainment spares computations, forward-positioned stock quantities, reorder points, and demand forecasts against reliability data and actual field consumption. Bring the recommendation and the assumptions behind it to the Logistics Program Manager, who sets the approved levels and reorder policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn failure data into provisioning updates. Work failure reporting and corrective action outputs into provisioning and sparing data. Flag high-failure components, recommend corrective logistics actions, and keep the provisioning baseline current as the design and test results evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Equipment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the support equipment data. Develop the support equipment recommendation data and the special tools baseline, and document the test, measurement, and diagnostic equipment and calibration requirements identified by Product Support Engineering&#39;s maintenance task and level of repair analyses. Where a support requirement could be engineered out rather than supported, flag it to Product Support Engineering and design engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Packaging, Handling, Storage &amp;amp; Transportation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop packaging, marking, and transportability data. Produce packaging data and special packaging instructions per MIL-STD-2073-1, marking per MIL-STD-129, and transportability documentation per MIL- STD-1366. Support container qualification and Performance Oriented Packaging certification, and support hazard classification submittals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop ammunition lifecycle documentation. Characterize shelf life and storage conditions; document handling, transportation, and storage constraints; compile surveillance and periodic inspection requirements; address demilitarization and disposal. Prepare ammunition data cards for missile deliveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across all three elements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform the analysis in the customer’s tools. Build models and generate customer reports using industry and government logistics software — Tempo (spares analysis) and SlicWave and Power Log-J (Logistics Product Data and supportability analysis), or equivalent. You are expected to become the program’s hands- on expert in this toolset, and to work fluently with the outputs of the level of repair and reliability analyses that Product Support Engineering produces in COMPASS, Relyence, or equivalent tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce contract deliverables. Author the assigned logistics deliverables for your three elements against government Data Item Descriptions on contractual due dates tied to design reviews. Prepare the content and supporting rationale that the Logistics Program Manager takes to the customer at each review, and draft the responses to government comments for the Logistics Program Manager&#39;s disposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support test and demonstration events. Contribute to logistics demonstration planning and execution, verifying that the specified tools, support equipment, and packaging are adequate against real hardware. Fold the findings back into the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the production transition. Partner with Product Support Engineering, Technical Publications, Packaging and Transportation, and Training to mature the support model behind a fielded munition, and help prepare the provisioning and packaging baseline for handoff as the program moves toward low-rate production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, logistics, supply chain, or a related technical field (equivalent military logistics experience may be substituted in lieu of education).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of product support, integrated logistics support, or sustainment experience in a military and/or defense industry environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of DoD Integrated Product Support and the twelve IPS elements, with hands-on depth in supply support, support equipment, and PHS&amp;amp;T.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing government logistics deliverables against Data Item Descriptions and CDRLs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with provisioning and cataloging: National Stock Number, CAGE code, part number structures, and provisioning parts lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with at least one logistics modeling or Logistics Product Data application — for example Power Log-J, SlicWave, Tempo, COMPASS, or Relyence — and the demonstrated ability to learn the rest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings, parts lists, and bills of material, and to work with design engineers to extract the logistics data you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct technical writing. This role produces formal documentation that a government customer reviews line by line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently on assigned deliverables in a fast-moving program environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel up to 25% domestically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Secret clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export-controlled information or facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with munitions, missiles, rockets, or energetic materials sustainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing ammunition lifecycle documentation and supporting hazard classification and storage planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with the standards governing this role’s scope — GEIA-STD-0007 (Logistics Product Data), MIL-STD-2073-1 (military packaging), MIL-STD-129 (marking), MIL-STD-1366 (transportability), and MIL-STD-130 (item identification and IUID).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with logistics management information data products or government logistics information systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a logistics demonstration, configuration audit, or first article inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Military background in an ordnance, ammunition, explosive ordnance disposal, or logistics role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a prototype-to-production transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with how FMECA, level of repair analysis, maintenance task analysis, and reliability-centered maintenance outputs drive provisioning, support equipment, and packaging decisions. This role consumes those analyses; Product Support Engineering produces them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$112,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$149,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an &lt;code&gt;@anduril.com&lt;/code&gt; address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:contact@anduril.com&quot;&gt;contact@anduril.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:contact@anduril.com&quot;&gt;contact@anduril.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a Mission Analyst to serve as Anduril’s tactical-level interface with the military operators&amp;nbsp;and planners who will employ our autonomous maritime systems. This is the person the customer works&amp;nbsp;with day-to-day — embedded in their environment, speaking their language, and ensuring our capability is&amp;nbsp;employed effectively.&lt;br&gt;This is not a desk job. You’ll be working alongside the customer, deployed on exercises, delivering training,&amp;nbsp;supporting mission planning, and feeding operational reality back into engineering. You’ll help shape how&amp;nbsp;the capability is used, how operators are trained, and how lessons from the field make it back to the people&amp;nbsp;building the system.&lt;br&gt;This position is available in Sydney, Australia. While based in Sydney, this role requires regular travel to&amp;nbsp;customer sites, exercises, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Support development of mission plans for exercises, demonstrations, operational test and evaluation,&amp;nbsp;and operational employment&lt;br&gt;• Provide tactical advice to customer planners on system capabilities, limitations, and employment options&lt;br&gt;• Develop and maintain tactical procedures, checklists, planning aids, and quick-reference materials&lt;br&gt;• Contribute to the development and refinement of Concepts of Employment (CONEMP) and Tactics,&amp;nbsp;Techniques and Procedures (TTPs)&lt;br&gt;• Support the training organisation in the delivery of operator training, including preparation of training&amp;nbsp;materials and subject matter support during course delivery&lt;br&gt;• Provide operational mentoring and tactical coaching to operators during exercises and employment&amp;nbsp;activities&lt;br&gt;• Plan and execute Anduril’s operational contribution to exercises and demonstrations&lt;br&gt;• Capture user feedback on system performance, usability, and employment concepts and translate it into&amp;nbsp;actionable input for engineering and product teams&lt;br&gt;• Identify gaps in procedures, training, or system capability from the operator’s perspective and advocate&amp;nbsp;for the user within Anduril&lt;br&gt;• Ensure operating procedures and training content reflect current employment concepts and real-world&amp;nbsp;operational patterns&lt;br&gt;• Build and maintain trusted peer-level relationships with customer operators and planners through&amp;nbsp;persistent presence and demonstrated competence&lt;br&gt;• Support post-exercise debriefs and lessons learned capture, feeding outcomes back into CONEMP,&amp;nbsp;TTPs, and training content&lt;br&gt;• Contribute operational input to program reporting and customer performance reviews&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience in operational planning, mission analysis, capability development, or a related field such as&lt;br&gt;defence, aviation, mining, or complex logistics&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated ability to work at the tactical level — translating system capabilities into practical&lt;br&gt;employment options&lt;br&gt;• Experience delivering training, instruction, or coaching in a Defence or technical context&lt;br&gt;• Strong interpersonal skills — able to build trust with military operators and planners as a credible peer&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable working autonomously in a customer environment with minimal direction&lt;br&gt;• Ability to translate complex system capabilities into clear operational language that users can act on&lt;br&gt;• Strong written communication — able to produce tactical procedures, planning aids, and operational&lt;br&gt;reports&lt;br&gt;• Eligible to obtain and maintain a Negative Vetting Level 2 (NV2) security clearance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Military background with operational experience in a maritime environment (submarine, surface warfare,&lt;br&gt;mine countermeasures, or equivalent)&lt;br&gt;• Experience with autonomous systems, unmanned platforms, or emerging military technology&lt;br&gt;• Experience in a Defence industry customer-facing role&lt;br&gt;• Knowledge of undersea warfare and maritime warfare concepts&lt;br&gt;• Understanding of Defence acquisition processes&lt;br&gt;• Experience contributing to Concept of Operations (CONOPS), CONEMP, or TTP development&lt;br&gt;• Experience with operational test and evaluation, exercise planning, or wargaming&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
